{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:acc5e23bc2409d650a891c6737176fe601245c73bee1218e1c7fd918a01c4b20","title":"Determine whether Quintom matter can support a nonzero minimum scale factor in Einstein gravity and then evolve above w = -1, allowing a possible connection to conventional expanding cosmology.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0000"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ac5e7548b50164b5d0209514ea66e0db6d23a9a7e5b52819a5e7fff72ec625c2","title":"Which NEC violations threaten the measurement and entropy arguments? The paper singles out stable propagating clock sectors that can approach non-gravitation, distinguishing them from quantum effects and projected objects that do not provide the same measuring apparatus.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0000"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ac38e43e81f3e3e268f8b96391eb8269c2da2f2f0f04179da496af612090e886","title":"How are Yang–Mills instantons, their zero modes and integration measures constructed, and how do they describe nonperturbative tunnelling, anomalous chiral interactions and Higgs suppression of large instantons?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0004"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:aca8ab4afd2917ca911b7d6b30a86b16e223118daffa8bf56a9fe9ed3b2922dd","title":"Can a dark-energy density determined by the future cosmological event horizon be represented by a canonical scalar obeying the assumed field-range bound?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0005"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:acfa3c138fe7f7b17c784ccfc8c8cea3c9281ba86224d642963559b38f4a1c7c","title":"Can a minimal moduli-plus-MSSM string effective theory generate flavor-suppressed soft terms, acceptable Higgs parameters, and gaugino masses while including supergravity quadratic divergences and tuning the cosmological constant?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0005"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ac0abc2e9c12bbf29b598967170e1aa57a4524459809c1eb2c95d29693d28dcd","title":"Which nonsupersymmetric AdS5×M6 compactifications on positive Kähler-Einstein six-manifolds are stable against linearized bosonic supergravity perturbations, and what do their KK spectrum, M5 nucleation channel and neutral massless scalars imply for possible instabilities?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0006"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ac833f8a2f16c94da090aea819f0f62d4bb59337f7e6789791dbf86698634146","title":"Under what geometric and perturbative conditions can type IIB LARGE Volume Scenarios stabilize Kähler moduli, and what inflationary and finite-temperature cosmology follows?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0007"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:acc4fe6ec3cf0578e3c50d83b9349b96dbac3de362d24b2ddb3a0daf5c0bcaad","title":"How can theory space be defined so that distances, convergence, disconnected components, boundedness and the information required to specify a QFT become precise? The broader objective is classification beyond perturbative Lagrangian descriptions.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0009"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ac36205563daf4202f4e9f37ea58874f0aeb0b9c3ee1f9e1a6d13a8779652faf","title":"Can late moduli decay simultaneously dilute excessive MSSM Affleck–Dine baryogenesis, produce the nonthermal LSP abundance, and explain the historical abundance ratio Ωdm/ΩB ≈ 5?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0011"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:ac87095276d62404026c0c6da0fc19781071efc07753429536d94e603cf9f5cc","title":"Can interacting quantum f